==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[begging]] [[the]] [[question]]|-}}

# A [[logical]] [[fallacy]] in which a [[premise]] of an [[argument]] contains a direct or indirect [[assumption]] that the [[conclusion]] is true; offering a [[circular argument]]; [[circular reasoning]].
#: ''It is an instance of '''begging the question''' to argue that God can only do good deeds because God is good.''

===Verb===
{{head|en|present participle}}

# {{context|informal|lang=en}} {{present participle of|beg the question|lang=en}}

====Usage notes====
In common usage '''begging the question''' is synonymous with "raising the question"; this usage is often [[proscribe]]d.

